<% content_for :title, "How this site works · #{current_family.name}" %>
<h1>How this site works</h1>
<p class="mut2">A short guide. Everything here can be changed later, and nothing you add is public: only people who were invited can see this site.</p>

<h2 id="start">The map</h2>
<ol class="map">
  <li><span class="n">1</span><div><strong>Add the people</strong><br><span class="fine">Everyone you know, even those who will never log in.</span><br><a href="<%= people_path %>">People</a></div></li>
  <li><span class="n">2</span><div><strong>Group them</strong><br><span class="fine">Into <%= terms.parties %> that answer together.</span><br><a href="<%= households_path %>"><%= terms.Parties %></a></div></li>
  <li><span class="n">3</span><div><strong>Find yourself</strong><br><span class="fine">Press <em>This is me</em> on your own name.</span><br><a href="<%= people_path %>">People</a></div></li>
  <li><span class="n">4</span><div><strong>Add your phone and mailing address</strong><br><span class="fine">On your own page, <em>Edit</em>.</span></div></li>
  <% if organizer? %><li><span class="n">5</span><div><strong>Invite those who should log in</strong><br><span class="fine">Organizers only.</span><br><a href="<%= admin_path %>">Admin</a></div></li><% end %>
  <li><span class="n"><%= organizer? ? 6 : 5 %></span><div><strong>Plan together</strong><br><span class="fine">Vote on dates, answer the RSVP, claim tasks, talk in the forum.</span><br><a href="<%= reunions_path %>"><%= terms.Events %></a></div></li>
</ol>

<h2>Where to start: add the people</h2>
<p><strong>Start by adding people.</strong> Everything else on this site hangs off the list of people: who answers the RSVP together, who is connected to whom, who gets a reminder, and who is invited to log in. So the first job is to get the right names in.</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Add the people you know.</strong> Open <a href="<%= people_path %>">People</a> and choose <em>Add a person</em>. You only need a first name; add a phone, email and mailing address if you have them. Add yourself and the people closest to you first.<% if terms.tree? %> To connect someone, open a person you already added and use <em>Add a parent</em>, <em>Add a partner</em> or <em>Add a child</em>. A child, a grandparent or anyone who will not log in can still be on the list.<% end %></li>
  <li><strong>Group them into <%= terms.parties %>.</strong> A <%= terms.party %> answers the RSVP together. Add people to one from the <a href="<%= households_path %>"><%= terms.Parties %></a> page.</li>
  <li><strong>Find yourself.</strong> Click your own name and press <em>This is me</em>. That connects your login to your entry so the site knows which <%= terms.party %> is yours.</li>
  <li><strong>Add your phone numbers and mailing address</strong> on your own page with <em>Edit</em>. The mailing address is where you get mail: a campus box or a different address from your <%= terms.party %> is fine. It belongs to you, not to your <%= terms.party %>.</li>
  <li><strong>Invite the people who should log in.</strong> Organizers do this from <a href="<%= admin_path %>">Admin</a> &rarr; Access; everyone else can ask an organizer.</li>
  <li><strong>Then answer the RSVP and vote on dates</strong> when a <%= terms.event %> is planned. The Home page shows what is waiting for you.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Updating your information</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Your contact details and address:</strong> People &rarr; your name &rarr; <em>Edit</em>.</li>
  <li><strong>The name other people see next to your messages:</strong> click your name at the top right of any page.</li>
  <li><strong>Keep something private:</strong> on <em>Edit</em>, tick the box at the bottom. Then only an organizer and that person can see their date of birth, notes, email, phone numbers and address.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Adding people later</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>One at a time:</strong> People &rarr; <em>Add a person</em>.</li>
  <li><strong>Someone who will log in:</strong> an organizer uses Admin &rarr; Access, and can add a new person right there.</li>
  <li><strong>Many at once:</strong> an organizer can import a spreadsheet from Admin.</li>
  <% if terms.tree? %><li><strong>The tree:</strong> the Tree page draws everyone you have connected.</li><% end %>
</ul>

<h2><%= terms.Events %>, dates, tasks and the forum</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong><%= terms.Events %>:</strong> open one to see the plan. When the dates are still being decided, <em>Vote</em> for every date that works for you.</li>
  <li><strong>RSVP:</strong> answer once for your <%= terms.party %>: how many adults and children, and any notes about food or a place to stay.</li>
  <li><strong>Tasks:</strong> claim something you can do. It shows who is handling what.</li>
  <li><strong>Calendar:</strong> every date in one place, with a link that adds it to your phone's calendar.</li>
  <li><strong>Forum:</strong> a place to talk. Start a topic or reply.</li>
  <li><strong>Reminders:</strong> you get at most one email a day, only when something needs you. Turn them off on <a href="<%= directory_path %>">Members</a>.</li>
</ul>

<% if organizer? %>
<h2>For organizers</h2>
<p class="mut2">Everything below is gathered on the <a href="<%= admin_path %>">Admin</a> page, which only organizers see.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Invite someone to log in:</strong> <a href="<%= members_path %>">Access</a>. Enter their email. If they are already in People, choose their name. If not, use <em>Not in the list? Add them here</em>.</li>
  <li><strong>Send a reminder to everyone:</strong> <a href="<%= new_announcement_path %>">Send a reminder</a>. You see who gets it before anything is sent.</li>
  <li><strong>Ask <%= terms.the_people %> a question, such as which dates work:</strong> <a href="<%= surveys_path %>">Surveys</a>. Write a few questions, preview who gets it, and everyone is emailed a personal link, even people without an account. You see the answers as they come in, and can turn the suggested dates into proposed dates for a vote.</li>
  <li><strong>Add many people at once:</strong> <a href="<%= import_people_path %>">Import from a spreadsheet</a>. Columns: First name, Last name, Phone, Email, Phone 2, Street 1, Street 2, City, State, Zip. You see a preview first, and anyone already on the list is skipped.</li>
  <li><strong>Download everyone:</strong> <a href="<%= export_people_path(format: :csv) %>">Download as a CSV</a>.</li>
</ul>
<% end %>

<h2>Stuck?</h2>
<p>Ask an organizer. They can see this same guide and can add or fix anything for you.</p>
